 "help.tips[0].examples[0].en": "even (weaker, better)",
 "help.tips[0].examples[1].en": "a multitude of",
 "help.tips[0].check.whyEn": "eine Vielzahl von is the formal choice; ein Haufen and ein Batzen are colloquial.",
 "help.tips[0].en.text": "Two words can mean the same and still not be interchangeable. The note on the back often names the plain or colloquial equivalent; learn which one fits a formal text.",
 "help.tips[0].en.title": "Register is part of the meaning",
 "help.tips[1].examples[0].en": "Even the boss was there.",
 "help.tips[1].examples[1].en": "Today of all days it's raining.",
 "help.tips[1].check.whyEn": "erst marks something as later than expected; nur marks it as less.",
 "help.tips[1].en.text": "selbst, sogar, ausgerechnet, erst, nur, lediglich, zumindest, erst recht: each one points at one word and says how surprising, small or large it is.",
 "help.tips[1].en.title": "Focus particles change what is stressed",
 "help.tips[2].examples[0].en": "Human dignity is inviolable.",
 "help.tips[2].examples[1].en": "The end does not justify the means.",
 "help.tips[2].check.whyEn": "das Gewissen: a noun from a Ge-… stem, neuter.",
 "help.tips[2].en.text": "die Vernunft, die Würde, das Gewissen, der Zweck, das Mittel: abstract ideas take der, die or das like any noun, and the ending is still the best clue.",
 "help.tips[2].en.title": "Abstract nouns still have a gender",
 "help.hookEn": "Gather the precise words of philosophy, science, law and literature, each with its article and its register.",
 "help.introEn": "Every word this module’s exercises use, on one deck of flashcards: 423 cards, 242 of them nouns. The vocabulary of this module is precise, stylistically marked vocabulary: register pairs, legal and philosophical terms, and fixed expressions, from the themes Philosophie & Gesellschaft, Wissenschaftssprache, Recht & Verwaltung: Amtsdeutsch, Literatur: Lyrik & Deutung. Write the German, choose it from four options, or flip the card and rate yourself. A word you miss comes back later in the same run, and stays in your weak words until you get it right three times in a row.",
 "help.rememberEn[0]": "Never say a noun without its article, not even in your head.",
 "help.rememberEn[1]": "Miss a word? It comes back in the same run. Three correct answers in a row take it off the weak list.",
 "help.rememberEn[2]": "Verbs and adjectives have no article: type them as they stand, like \"selbst\"."
}